《最后一场皮影戏》 (The Last Shadow Play) — a film in the Chinese Shadow Puppetry style, made entirely in code.

Story, puppets (the master, the boy, the Monkey King, the White Bone Demon in both forms, the crowd), scenery, carving patterns, staging,
camera, melodies and sound design are original and generated by the code in this folder. The legend of the Monkey King and the White Bone
Demon is public-domain folklore (Journey to the West, 16th century). Traditional motifs (fish-scale armour, cloud scrolls, meander, coin and
lattice patterns, the opera face mark) are used generically; no historical puppet is copied.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/)
- Ma Shan Zheng — Copyright 2018 The Ma Shan Zheng Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/mashanzheng) — titles, plaques, seals
- Noto Serif SC — Copyright 2017 The Noto Project Authors (https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk) — placards and sheet labels
- Cormorant Garamond — Copyright 2015 The Cormorant Project Authors (https://github.com/CatharsisFonts/Cormorant) — loaded, Latin only
  The font files were taken from the @fontsource npm packages (unicode-range slices).

Music: original score (music/score.py). Sampled instruments through the library's core/audio/sampler.py, all CC0 1.0:
- VSCO 2 Community Edition (Versilian Studios): crash cymbals, concert bass drum, log drum, flute, oboe
- Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios): gong, suspended cymbal, woodblock, frame drum
- Karoryfer Samples / sfzinstruments (aliexpress-erhu): erhu (used as a banhu-like fiddle)
- Plucked strings: physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, shamisen preset, used as a sanxian-like pluck)

Sound effects and ambience: synthesized (numpy; core/audio/sfx.py and mix.py). No voice.

Tools: Chromium (headless), WebGL2, ffmpeg (two-pass loudnorm to −14 LUFS).
